A||||6||jlhuber||what to do with the old 2.8?||||5||
Z||000000||jlhuber||08-06-2000||02:47 AM||||anyone know if a 2.8 from the fiero will fit into a s-10?  it is the same basic block right?  now i am sure that some things will have to be modified or changed, like adding an electric cooling fan to the s-10, but what all is required?  i am going to be doing the 3800s/c conversion soon so i will have the 2.8 just lying around.  my uncle has a 92 s-10 4cyl 5spd with a bad motor that he says i can have.  basically, as the first line of this post says, i am curious as to if i can stuf my 2.8 into it with minimal efforts.  thanks<P>                         -jess||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2000||10:34 AM||||It's the same block, only the 'bolt on's" are different. You'll have to use all the brackets off the S-10, the fan assembly will bolt to the water pump on the Fiero engine or you can buy a new one. (recommended). If the S-10 is MPI it will be a stright swap, other wise you have two choices: change the intake's or change the wiring harness and computer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||08-07-2000||06:52 PM||||The GM crate 3.4 is intended to replace a 2.8 in an S10. To use it in a Fiero the starter holes have to be drilled in the opposite side. I'm assuming that means the starter is on the opposite side on an S10 2.8???||||reg||5
Z||000003||fierocrazy||08-08-2000||08:55 AM||||blocks are the same except oil filter location, i beleive it was differant because the 4 wheel drive version. not sure about the 2 wheel drive might be a crossmember problem. my .02||||reg||1
Z||000004||triker||08-08-2000||07:23 PM||||I know for a fact that the starter is on the wrong side, I was going to do the same swap, except I was going to replace an existing 2.8 blazer with a Fiero 2.8.  I ended up saving the low milage 87 Fiero engine (4,000 miles)and putting a used 2.8 out of an S-10 P.U. in my Blazer.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSTETZ||08-08-2000||07:27 PM||||if you can't find a use for it, i am currently looking for a 2.8 that can be rebuilt. let me know if you are interested in selling it, or maybe just tossing it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (tell me where though!)||||reg||1
